sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ESP32 as ESP32 Client
    participant Server as FastAPI OTA Server
    participant CA as Offline Root CA (ca.crt / ca.key)

    Note over Server, CA: Handled once on server (or on signing key rotation)
    CA->>Server: Signs Certificate (signing.crt) using ca.key

    Note over ESP32, Server: PHASE 1: HANDSHAKE & MANIFEST CHECK
    ESP32->>Server: GET /api/v1/ota/check <br> Headers: Device API Key, Version, HW ID, Device ID, Channel, HSVN
    Server->>Server: Checks release registry for Channel <br> Validates HSVN boundary condition <br> Evaluates deterministic Canary target logic
    Server-->>ESP32: Returns Payload: url, update_type, signature, target_signature, signing_cert (PEM)

    Note over ESP32: PHASE 2: VERIFICATION & STREAMING
    ESP32->>ESP32: mbedtls_x509_crt_verify() <br> Validate signing_cert against embedded ca.crt
    alt Certificate Chain is Invalid
        ESP32->>ESP32: Abort Update (Reject untrusted signature authority)
    else Certificate Chain is Valid
        ESP32->>ESP32: Extract Public Key from verified signing_cert
        ESP32->>Server: GET /firmware_storage/patches/patch.bin?token=...
        Server-->>ESP32: Stream Binary Payload in Chunks
        ESP32->>ESP32: Decompress & Write to Flash (ota_next)
        ESP32->>ESP32: Calculate SHA-256 of written partition data
        ESP32->>ESP32: mbedtls_pk_verify() <br> Verify hash against target_signature using Public Key
        alt Signature is Invalid
            ESP32->>ESP32: Abort & Erase partition (Prevent corrupt/malicious execution)
            ESP32->>Server: POST /api/v1/ota/status (failure, error_code)
        else Signature is Valid
            ESP32->>ESP32: Set Active Boot Partition & Reboot
            ESP32->>Server: POST /api/v1/ota/status (success)
            Note over Server: Server monitors status reports and applies auto-rollback if failure limits breached
        end
    end
